[{:db/id "q-107545/selection/087d2cf0d63fc4dcfbd3a93fa95fbfa301763b46a4de0e9362193e95de2fb250" :answer/id #uuid "3a979f27-5eed-5578-b130-f63c0032ad33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107545/selection/886e2cd9465e72449c46bf7ec61593bf4276aa340116021f8158f687b877f78a" :answer/id #uuid "7aacdd41-ec92-529b-a070-c36dff0f9e7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107545/selection/7a1ddcd198fe29c120a4ee0c30f9cdd5cb60a39302b9e719960dca99ebd98eff" :answer/id #uuid "e08c910a-da01-5914-a54f-dd29480ef77d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107545/selection/9d67117f0564ec0787374cfee26b11277f52f45f76540dfc97a3c627537f970b" :answer/id #uuid "c08c54b0-c058-57bf-8046-b30d81e440a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107545/selection/31b8ebd8f1c90cdd68acaa9b9a3e44b304f0b2f4c62aed961bf6f01589cb7d32" :answer/id #uuid "00e9ee47-8163-514f-8c70-e64bd59d74d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107545/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6c8a277-2073-577b-a7cd-16a08da84faa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107545/selection/087d2cf0d63fc4dcfbd3a93fa95fbfa301763b46a4de0e9362193e95de2fb250" :answer-field/choices ["q-107545/selection/087d2cf0d63fc4dcfbd3a93fa95fbfa301763b46a4de0e9362193e95de2fb250" "q-107545/selection/886e2cd9465e72449c46bf7ec61593bf4276aa340116021f8158f687b877f78a" "q-107545/selection/7a1ddcd198fe29c120a4ee0c30f9cdd5cb60a39302b9e719960dca99ebd98eff" "q-107545/selection/9d67117f0564ec0787374cfee26b11277f52f45f76540dfc97a3c627537f970b" "q-107545/selection/31b8ebd8f1c90cdd68acaa9b9a3e44b304f0b2f4c62aed961bf6f01589cb7d32"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107545" :question/id #uuid "3416f819-c147-56ca-a73a-756cccad298c" :question/math-academy-id "q-107545" :question/problem "Given that $x=5$ is a solution to the equation ${x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+29x-45=0,$ find the remaining solutions." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+29x-45.$ Since $x=5$ is a root of $f(x),$ then according to the factor theorem $(x-5)$ is a factor of $f(x).$ \n\nWe find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by $(x-5)$ using synthetic division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\enclose{bottom right}{5} & 1 & -9 & 29 & -45 \\\\  &  & 5 & -20 & 45 \\\\  & 1 & -4 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $f(x)=(x-5)({x}^{2}-4x+9).$ \n\nTo find the remaining two roots, we solve ${x}^{2}-4x+9=0$ by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+4+5 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =-5 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{5}\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\text{i} \\\\ x & =2\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to our original equation are $x=5,\\,2\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107545/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f10a926-3cfd-5575-ae19-59f95cdca45f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107545"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-104500"] :question/problem "Given that $x=-\\frac{1}{4}$ is a solution to the equation $36{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}+4x+1=0,$ find the remaining solutions." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=36{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}+4x+1.$ Since $x=-\\frac{1}{4}$ is a root of $f(x),$ then according to the factor theorem $(x+\\frac{1}{4})$ is a factor of $f(x).$ \n\nWe find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by $(x+\\frac{1}{4})$ using synthetic division.\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{4}$ | $36$ | $9$ | $4$ | $1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-9$ | $0$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $36$ | $0$ | $4$ | $0$ |\n\nThus, $f(x)=(x+\\frac{1}{4})(36{x}^{2}+4).$ \n\nTo find the remaining two roots, we solve $36{x}^{2}+4=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36{x}^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ 36{x}^{2} & =-4 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-\\frac{1}{9} \\\\ {x}^{2} & ={(\\frac{1}{3}\\text{i})}^{2} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{1}{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to our original equation are $x=-\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{3}\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-317978/field-1/d17c1231a58f15a4aec7a4cc5b3add05a7989eb3ebdfbcc43e5f8c92f795de7b" :answer/id #uuid "3ab9c5a9-5607-5462-9e6a-27fcf3281e1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317978/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7706a19-8962-5c0e-ab22-27413dfcd17e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317978/field-1/d17c1231a58f15a4aec7a4cc5b3add05a7989eb3ebdfbcc43e5f8c92f795de7b" :answer-field/choices ["q-317978/field-1/d17c1231a58f15a4aec7a4cc5b3add05a7989eb3ebdfbcc43e5f8c92f795de7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317978" :question/id #uuid "befb63f6-09c7-53f3-a3d5-95104472d1e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-317978" :question/problem "Given that $x=-\\frac{1}{4}$ is a solution to the equation $4{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+100x+25=0,$ find the remaining solutions.\n\n$x=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=4{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+100x+25.$ Since $x=-\\frac{1}{4}$ is a root of $f(x),$ then according to the factor theorem $(x+\\frac{1}{4})$ is a factor of $f(x).$ \n\nWe find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by $(x+\\frac{1}{4})$ using synthetic division.\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{4}$ | $4$ | $1$ | $100$ | $25$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $-25$ |\n|  | $4$ | $0$ | $100$ | $0$ |\n\nThus, $f(x)=(x+\\frac{1}{4})(4{x}^{2}+100).$ \n\nTo find the remaining two roots, we solve $4{x}^{2}+100=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+100 & =0 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =-100 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-25 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =(5\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ x & =\\pm 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to our original equation are $x=-\\frac{1}{4},\\,\\pm 5\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317978/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f10a926-3cfd-5575-ae19-59f95cdca45f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317978"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-17409/selection/d89db0ec678b0a0746cc62ee7288bba8f45be141ed708a0118a0fda8149c04bf" :answer/id #uuid "8286d7c8-a8e5-5c7f-89b7-3a1aa6d3bdac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pm 3\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17409/selection/3556c530136f0085a3a76b3eee543718242d1448e37beef27cae21e2ac0af438" :answer/id #uuid "67942167-2577-583d-8cf6-3042ee870463" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pm 4\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17409/selection/2dd29a2e8e0c3b5fb56e93adc8585d698348d688f15fcf85646ad3408c0f5374" :answer/id #uuid "e56f057f-f61f-51d8-99dd-3a415f8cb38e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17409/selection/bd2cf4814837b19f40cd2f734edb0a5545bd1652855c8b09bb04145e3ce9c089" :answer/id #uuid "d95f989f-c2d4-5422-a6b9-7760ecb85bde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pm 3\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17409/selection/d36c2e34debe4cc2ef6b7857f79e762dd320870673e3a243ca47d11f1b713447" :answer/id #uuid "abd8a9c2-9326-5f80-8d62-99ce9348339c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pm 2\\sqrt{5}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17409/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1e03f55-9e8e-5d3f-b579-70c85ecbe37c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-17409/selection/2dd29a2e8e0c3b5fb56e93adc8585d698348d688f15fcf85646ad3408c0f5374" :answer-field/choices ["q-17409/selection/d89db0ec678b0a0746cc62ee7288bba8f45be141ed708a0118a0fda8149c04bf" "q-17409/selection/3556c530136f0085a3a76b3eee543718242d1448e37beef27cae21e2ac0af438" "q-17409/selection/2dd29a2e8e0c3b5fb56e93adc8585d698348d688f15fcf85646ad3408c0f5374" "q-17409/selection/bd2cf4814837b19f40cd2f734edb0a5545bd1652855c8b09bb04145e3ce9c089" "q-17409/selection/d36c2e34debe4cc2ef6b7857f79e762dd320870673e3a243ca47d11f1b713447"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17409" :question/id #uuid "0cf02442-8d73-58e6-a299-ebbbd1788a53" :question/math-academy-id "q-17409" :question/problem "Given that $x=-10$ is a solution to the equation ${x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-24x+160=0,$ find the remaining solutions." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-24x+160.$ Since $x=-10$ is a root of $f(x),$ then according to the factor theorem $(x+10)$ is a factor of $f(x).$ \n\nWe find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by $(x+10)$ using synthetic division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\enclose{bottom right}{-10} & 1 & 6 & -24 & 160 \\\\  &  & -10 & 40 & -160 \\\\  & 1 & -4 & 16 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $f(x)=(x+10)({x}^{2}-4x+16).$ \n\nTo find the remaining two roots, we solve ${x}^{2}-4x+16=0$ by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+16 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+4+12 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+12 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =-12 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}\\text{i} \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to our original equation are $x=-10,\\,2\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-17409/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f10a926-3cfd-5575-ae19-59f95cdca45f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17409"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104497/selection/31b8ebd8f1c90cdd68acaa9b9a3e44b304f0b2f4c62aed961bf6f01589cb7d32" :answer/id #uuid "455737fa-8f9a-5c53-9c32-0e89354e4b0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104497/selection/8f097184f7ab4ece6eeeffbc23603fe5c221f363299e3efec51b55da0803a839" :answer/id #uuid "adde2b37-c2fa-57f9-82a7-11b7925d1c38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104497/selection/99d93f46de826941ee2a0e6a5510824bd6c2f2fd2353a30c5cc07989508bc562" :answer/id #uuid "1e51a76e-05c7-5669-bcc7-f5f410503352" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\pm \\frac{1}{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104497/selection/ea2086a3b78f9587ba8daaf4246322826f6c555b30fd02dd8dcae39f2aa9d743" :answer/id #uuid "eeba1ff4-0775-53e9-a7fa-0bfccf059128" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104497/selection/d23846d7c6c8d92f27737a7a7dbbe9029dfa40971f4cc6ff3a119ba988e7dc1e" :answer/id #uuid "8d8bee53-4dd6-5937-be20-fb0df3a13e79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\pm \\frac{1}{3}\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104497/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b393ecb0-87e2-5c0d-b32a-76f10eae3e34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104497/selection/31b8ebd8f1c90cdd68acaa9b9a3e44b304f0b2f4c62aed961bf6f01589cb7d32" :answer-field/choices ["q-104497/selection/31b8ebd8f1c90cdd68acaa9b9a3e44b304f0b2f4c62aed961bf6f01589cb7d32" "q-104497/selection/8f097184f7ab4ece6eeeffbc23603fe5c221f363299e3efec51b55da0803a839" "q-104497/selection/99d93f46de826941ee2a0e6a5510824bd6c2f2fd2353a30c5cc07989508bc562" "q-104497/selection/ea2086a3b78f9587ba8daaf4246322826f6c555b30fd02dd8dcae39f2aa9d743" "q-104497/selection/d23846d7c6c8d92f27737a7a7dbbe9029dfa40971f4cc6ff3a119ba988e7dc1e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104497" :question/id #uuid "bbb34119-16b7-5bfa-b1df-ad34b590b96b" :question/math-academy-id "q-104497" :question/problem "Given that $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ is a solution to the equation $3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+8x-2=0,$ find the remaining solutions." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=9{x}^{3}-21{x}^{2}+24x-6.$ Since $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ is a root of $f(x),$ then according to the factor theorem $(x-\\frac{1}{3})$ is a factor of $f(x).$ \n\nWe find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by $(x-\\frac{1}{3})$ using synthetic division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\enclose{bottom right}{\\frac{1}{3}} & 3 & -7 & 8 & -2 \\\\  &  & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\  & 3 & -6 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $f(x)=(x-\\frac{1}{3})(3{x}^{2}-6x+6).$ \n\nTo find the remaining two roots, we solve $3{x}^{2}-6x+6=0$ by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-6x+6 & =0 \\\\ 3({x}^{2}-2x+2) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+2 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+1+1 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =(\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ x & =1\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to our original equation are $x=\\frac{1}{3},\\,1\\pm \\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104497/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f10a926-3cfd-5575-ae19-59f95cdca45f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104497"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-101758"] :question/problem "Find all of the solutions to $2{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+20x-8=0$ given that $x=2-2\\text{i}$ is a solution." :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+20x-8.$ \n\nSince $f(x)$ has real coefficients and ${x}_{1}=2-2\\text{i}$ is a root of $f(x),$ the complex conjugate \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}_{1}}=\\overset{―}{2-2\\text{i}}=2+2\\text{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root of $f(x).$\n\nNow, according to the factor theorem, \n$(x-(2-2\\text{i}))(x-(2+2\\text{i}))$\nis a factor of $f(x).$ Expanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-(2-2\\text{i}))(x-(2+2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-(2-2\\text{i}+2+2\\text{i})x+(2-2\\text{i})(2+2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+({2}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+8 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by ${x}^{2}-4x+8$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-1 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-4x+8\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+20x-8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+16x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}+4x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}+4x-8}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}-4x+8)(2x-1).$ \n\nTo find the remaining root, we set the linear factor equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-1=0\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=\\frac{1}{2},2\\pm 2\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-104514/selection/c620480639fabe94d331b2bb59effa38b268878d6c214a581b47723b12ce5189" :answer/id #uuid "0162a096-183a-5bdb-b167-ac7db62e2786" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2,0,3-\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104514/selection/97f927157e88b08dcd270b9984c45a711f329d37c7a003e51927d2db3804b75d" :answer/id #uuid "a7d4803a-4caa-5055-9714-ac773f698278" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2,3\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104514/selection/ed8ba4356c2963476e7cf96c33144dc2b53c666ba0adfbe7b47a425660da2403" :answer/id #uuid "a9851d43-c8fa-5651-be51-cf276eb13d4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 2,3-\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104514/selection/0d70edc004f0a2287071ef7bce37389a6663710d6ae3993ce002353f1dc34e39" :answer/id #uuid "543b8056-a152-55ea-b4f0-c37e96cdcda7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2,3\\pm \\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104514/selection/b6a646e84ce952601bf270920ec796a5de6e77e4c91de568a0ce167fe8c07b37" :answer/id #uuid "deb451b3-1cd7-524c-bd2d-f02d71bae83c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0,3-\\text{i},1+3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104514/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f4d0c9a-78d1-525e-87e4-8a5e9d36fa42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104514/selection/0d70edc004f0a2287071ef7bce37389a6663710d6ae3993ce002353f1dc34e39" :answer-field/choices ["q-104514/selection/c620480639fabe94d331b2bb59effa38b268878d6c214a581b47723b12ce5189" "q-104514/selection/97f927157e88b08dcd270b9984c45a711f329d37c7a003e51927d2db3804b75d" "q-104514/selection/ed8ba4356c2963476e7cf96c33144dc2b53c666ba0adfbe7b47a425660da2403" "q-104514/selection/0d70edc004f0a2287071ef7bce37389a6663710d6ae3993ce002353f1dc34e39" "q-104514/selection/b6a646e84ce952601bf270920ec796a5de6e77e4c91de568a0ce167fe8c07b37"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104514" :question/id #uuid "f46539e8-9ace-5c88-b4d4-dec07a27569b" :question/math-academy-id "q-104514" :question/problem "Find all of the solutions to ${x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-2x+20=0$ given that $x=3-\\text{i}$ is a solution." :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(x)={x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-2x+20.$ \n\nSince $f(x)$ has real coefficients and ${x}_{1}=3-\\text{i}$ is a root of $f(x),$ the complex conjugate \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}_{1}}=\\overset{―}{3-\\text{i}}=3+\\text{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root of $f(x).$\n\nNow, according to the factor theorem, \n$(x-(3-\\text{i}))(x-(3+\\text{i}))$\nis a factor of $f(x).$ Expanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-(3-\\text{i}))(x-(3+\\text{i})) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-(3-\\text{i}+(3+\\text{i)})x+(3-\\text{i})(3+\\text{i}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x+({3}^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x+10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by ${x}^{2}-6x+10$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+2 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-6x+10\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-2x+20} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-12x+20 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}-12x+20}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n     \n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}-6x+10)(x+2).$ \n\nTo find the remaining root, we set the linear factor equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2=0\\,⟹\\,x=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=-2,3\\pm \\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-104514/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9dc69a9e-6344-5a92-beb7-0c9fef8171d3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104514"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107548/selection/c3143b1bb8fb8b189e0be3c9f7642a3dbfb65ee367f1bbc8a907a75865c1e265" :answer/id #uuid "dcc1a1d8-ca8f-51b0-86f3-04c924a8180c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1,\\pm 3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107548/selection/a34c1766d9db3a1cc73b6d56118549d136f1d4bd71eafc3ec4f84d0d440a7b5d" :answer/id #uuid "896bae99-bfc5-5d93-8aab-2116eabc6011" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2,\\pm 3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107548/selection/fa7b1f3f7c9ef2e1281760b1868919f31a42566888460cfa2a9ae54453eb05f9" :answer/id #uuid "75dc36bf-36ec-5d8f-9d42-43dfcc1f2532" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1,3,3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107548/selection/451f6167dcb6a36feb83ef2c04e0070ab4741d1aec8aefb24115a2edd3eb63e5" :answer/id #uuid "b7ae4198-e5e5-5c93-941b-c13b80d3e03a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3,\\pm 3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107548/selection/13527efd9a30d94b96f2e9f7ba923daa9ebb483daedb186916a4187f161491de" :answer/id #uuid "414c2ee4-cb13-5e5b-bf64-75d82d3f856f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1,2,3\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107548/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50cc86fd-84ec-5f56-a3b1-bab9059e6fce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107548/selection/c3143b1bb8fb8b189e0be3c9f7642a3dbfb65ee367f1bbc8a907a75865c1e265" :answer-field/choices ["q-107548/selection/c3143b1bb8fb8b189e0be3c9f7642a3dbfb65ee367f1bbc8a907a75865c1e265" "q-107548/selection/a34c1766d9db3a1cc73b6d56118549d136f1d4bd71eafc3ec4f84d0d440a7b5d" "q-107548/selection/fa7b1f3f7c9ef2e1281760b1868919f31a42566888460cfa2a9ae54453eb05f9" "q-107548/selection/451f6167dcb6a36feb83ef2c04e0070ab4741d1aec8aefb24115a2edd3eb63e5" "q-107548/selection/13527efd9a30d94b96f2e9f7ba923daa9ebb483daedb186916a4187f161491de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107548" :question/id #uuid "d8957c2b-9ff3-53f8-83c1-0ad5de59519d" :question/math-academy-id "q-107548" :question/problem "Find all of the solutions to ${x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+9x-9=0$ given that $x=-3\\text{i}$ is a solution." :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(x)={x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+9x-9.$ \n\nSince $f(x)$ has real coefficients and ${x}_{1}=-3\\text{i}$ is a root of $f(x),$ the complex conjugate \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}_{1}}=\\overset{―}{-3\\text{i}}=3\\text{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root of $f(x).$\n\nNow, according to the factor theorem, \n$(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i}))$\nis a factor of $f(x).$ Expanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) & ={x}^{2}+(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by ${x}^{2}+9$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-1\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & {x}^{2}+9\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+9x-9\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+9x}_{―} \\\\  & -{x}^{2}\\,\\,-9 \\\\  & \\,{-\\,{x}^{2}\\,\\,-9}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}+9)(x-1).$ \n\nTo find the remaining root, we set the linear factor equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-1=0\\,⟹\\,x=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=1,\\pm 3\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107548/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9dc69a9e-6344-5a92-beb7-0c9fef8171d3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107548"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104516/selection/a2703e2b55f8f32a59b198549d8d08c805487d4c59d5b1eaef04ebd387a857c9" :answer/id #uuid "067119f7-1bfb-5e89-97a4-0a56ea3c3710" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 4,-5+2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104516/selection/6196844faf7bba082909296a37e239fef099e4d855dc716555d33038531d0b61" :answer/id #uuid "1e228e50-14d0-5013-bb46-64fb20792755" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4,-5\\pm 2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104516/selection/216e85734de61ea9db62b3f621fa1d53df3a10abdc7e17870393e391fde87ba8" :answer/id #uuid "b75513b2-10b8-518b-9b52-6ef6a78b844c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-4,-5\\pm 2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104516/selection/434afe6bf385952262e9f37d27d185bc15b8fb97e473ca2dd17ccdc56ac7af33" :answer/id #uuid "f48e3d00-70bb-5aa8-be87-5511459174e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-4,0,-5+2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104516/selection/62d447e9625049c91c7c2115528c983ace534e6204e32c60b8763186addf61ab" :answer/id #uuid "04b18ffd-5215-509a-9893-39bb39e967d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0,4,-5+2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104516/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "286b9f8e-928f-5607-a71f-9eb67ce9bff9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104516/selection/6196844faf7bba082909296a37e239fef099e4d855dc716555d33038531d0b61" :answer-field/choices ["q-104516/selection/a2703e2b55f8f32a59b198549d8d08c805487d4c59d5b1eaef04ebd387a857c9" "q-104516/selection/6196844faf7bba082909296a37e239fef099e4d855dc716555d33038531d0b61" "q-104516/selection/216e85734de61ea9db62b3f621fa1d53df3a10abdc7e17870393e391fde87ba8" "q-104516/selection/434afe6bf385952262e9f37d27d185bc15b8fb97e473ca2dd17ccdc56ac7af33" "q-104516/selection/62d447e9625049c91c7c2115528c983ace534e6204e32c60b8763186addf61ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104516" :question/id #uuid "11ab4f0c-a250-5489-90e6-0b0b8a5999d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-104516" :question/problem "Find all of the solutions to ${x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-11x-116=0$ given that $x=-5+2\\text{i}$ is a solution." :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(x)={x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-11x-116.$\n\nSince $f(x)$ has real coefficients and ${x}_{1}=-5+2\\text{i}$ is a root of $f(x),$ the complex conjugate \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}_{1}}=\\overset{―}{-5+2\\text{i}}=-5-2\\text{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root of $f(x).$\n\nNow, according to the factor theorem, \n$(x-(-5+2\\text{i}))(x-(-5-2\\text{i}))$\nis a factor of $f(x).$ Expanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-(-5+2\\text{i}))(x-(-5-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-(-5+2\\text{i}+(-5-2\\text{i)})x+(-5+2\\text{i})(-5-2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+10x+((-5)^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}+10x+29 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by ${x}^{2}+10x+29$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-4 \\\\  & {x}^{2}+10x+29\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-11x-116} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+10{x}^{2}+29x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,-4{x}^{2}+40x-116 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,{-4{x}^{2}+40x-116}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n        \n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}+10x+29)(x-4).$ \n\nTo find the remaining root, we set the linear factor equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-4=0\\,⟹\\,x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=4,-5\\pm 2\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-104516/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9dc69a9e-6344-5a92-beb7-0c9fef8171d3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104516"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317986/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "4ffa7934-b256-534d-9750-eabde4b512bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317986/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "749dd247-28ca-5b74-9f06-5989bc4372ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317986/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-317986/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317986/field-2/d17c1231a58f15a4aec7a4cc5b3add05a7989eb3ebdfbcc43e5f8c92f795de7b" :answer/id #uuid "fb7929e8-4ee8-5377-b930-314c1224be2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317986/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c308244-90cf-530d-8c47-5d6bf7eb1e77" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317986/field-2/d17c1231a58f15a4aec7a4cc5b3add05a7989eb3ebdfbcc43e5f8c92f795de7b" :answer-field/choices ["q-317986/field-2/d17c1231a58f15a4aec7a4cc5b3add05a7989eb3ebdfbcc43e5f8c92f795de7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317986" :question/id #uuid "177f798f-98fb-53b0-bae4-ba0d79693695" :question/math-academy-id "q-317986" :question/problem "Determine all the solutions to ${x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+25x-25=0$ given that $x=5\\text{i}$ is a solution. Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=\\pm $\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(x)={x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+25x-25.$ \n\nSince $f(x)$ has real coefficients and ${x}_{1}=5\\text{i}$ is a root of $f(x),$ the complex conjugate \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{{x}_{1}}=\\overset{―}{5\\text{i}}=-5\\text{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root of $f(x).$\n\nNow, according to the factor theorem, $(x-5\\text{i})(x-(-5\\text{i}))$ is a factor of $f(x).$ Expanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-5\\text{i})(x-(-5\\text{i})) & ={x}^{2}+(5\\text{i})(-5\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by ${x}^{2}+25$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-1\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & {x}^{2}+25\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+25x-25\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+25x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}\\,-25 \\\\  & \\,\\,{\\,-{x}^{2}\\,\\,-25}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}+25)(x-1).$ \n\nTo find the remaining root, we set the linear factor equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-1=0\\,⟹\\,x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=1$ and $x=\\pm \\,5\\text{i}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317986/field-1" "q-317986/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9dc69a9e-6344-5a92-beb7-0c9fef8171d3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317986"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5794"] :question/problem "Given that $x=-2$ is a solution to the equation $x^3+8 = 0,$ find the remaining solutions." :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x) = x^3+8.$ Since $x=-2$ is a root of $f(x),$ then according to the factor theorem $(x+2)$ is a factor of $f(x).$ \n\nWe find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by $(x+2)$ using synthetic division.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065202/assets/a92f1e322fc91c8388e7969117aca8e616625128d82ee12c88ce108cb6b2637e.png)\n\nThus, $f(x) = (x+2)(x^2-2x+4).$ \n\nTo find the remaining two roots, we solve $x^2-2x+4 = 0$ by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+1+3 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+3 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =-3 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})}^{2} \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i} \\\\ x & =1\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to our original equation are $x=-2, \\, 1\\pm \\sqrt3\\textrm{i}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8800"] :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(x) = x^3-3x^2+12x-10.$ \n\nSince $f(x)$ has real coefficients and $x_1=1+3\\text{i}$ is a root of $f(x),$ the complex conjugate \n\n$$\n\\overline{x_1}=\\overline{1+3\\textrm{i}}=1-3\\text{i}\n$$\n\nmust also be a root of $f(x).$\n\nNow, according to the factor theorem, \n$\\big(x-(1+3\\text{i})\\big)\\big(x-(1-3\\text{i})\\big)$\nis a factor of $f(x).$ Expanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-(1+3\\text{i}))(x-(1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-(1+3\\text{i}+1-3\\text{i})x+(1+3\\text{i})(1-3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+({1}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by $x^2 - 2x + 10$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-1 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-2x+10\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+12x-10\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}+2x-10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,-\\,{x}^{2}+2x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $f(x) = (x^2 - 2x + 10)(x-1).$ \n\nTo find the remaining root, we set the linear factor equal to zero and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-1=0\\,⟹\\,x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the roots are $x=1, 1 \\pm 3\\textrm{i}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
